.TH MKDIR 1
.SH NAME
mkdir \- make a directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkdir
[
.B \-p
]
.I dirname ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Mkdir
creates the specified directories.
.PP
If the
.B \-p
flag is given,
.I mkdir
creates any necessary parent directories
and does not complain if the target directory already exists.
The flag is recognised only as the first argument.
.SH SOURCE
.B cmd/mkdir/main.odin
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR rm (1),
.IR open (2)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.I Mkdir
returns an empty exit status if all directories were made.
Otherwise it prints a diagnostic for each that was not
and returns
.BR "can't make" .
Without
.BR \-p ,
a directory that already exists is an error.
.SH BUGS
There is no
.B \-m
flag.
A directory is made with mode 0777 or with what its server chooses.
